INT. BOWLING ALLEY - LANE 12 - NIGHT

Neon pins. Disco ball dull with grease. A league night. Leather shoes squeak on wax.

The tenth frame. Final game of the championship. Lane 12 holds three people and a hush.

MARCEL "THE HAMMER" DUBOIS (50s, belly, wristband, ball already in hand) steps to the line. His rival, GERTRUDE "GERT" NAKAMURA-HOLT (60s, sleeveless, forearms like cables) leans on the ball return, arms crossed, scowling. Their referee, DELPHINE ARCHAMBEAU (30s, clipboard, whistle around her neck) stands between them, tally sheet trembling in her hands.

DELPHINE
Marcel needs a spare for the win.

GERT
He needs a miracle.

MARCEL
Silence, please.

He raises the ball to his chin. Closes his eyes. Steps. Swings. Releases. The ball rolls, wobbles, drifts, and curves wide of the head pin. Seven pins fall. Three stand: left, right, center.

DELPHINE
Seven.

GERT
(smirking)
Called it.

Marcel stands rigid. The ball returns. He catches it and, without a word, wheels around, lifts it high, and hurls it. It crashes into the ball return, bounces, spins across the lane, skids into the gutter, and strikes a standing pin from the side. All three tumble. Pinsetter whirs. Gert throws up both arms, Delphine drops her clipboard, Marcel looks at his empty hands as if he is not sure they are his.

A long silence. Then Delphine laughs. Gert laughs. Marcel, shaking, laughs loudest of all.

DELPHINE
That is not legal. That is absolutely not legal.

GERT
It counts.

MARCEL
Does it?

DELPHINE
(exhaling)
It counts.

Gert extends a hand. Marcel takes it. They shake, too long, too hard, then both let go and grab their lanes' ball return, smiling stupidly.

GERT
Next year, I destroy you.

MARCEL
I look forward to it.
